  8.7 PSON_L INPUT
     The PSON_L is an internally pulled-up (3.3 V) input signal to enable/disable the main output V1 of the front-end. This active-
     low pin is also used to clear any latched fault condition. The timing diagram is given Figure 29 and the parameters in Table 5.


                                                        OPERATING CONDITION                                     MIN           MAX               UNIT
                                     tPSON_L V1on                 PSON_L to V1 delay (on)                        2              20                  ms
                                     tPSON_L V1off                PSON_L to V1 delay (off)                       2              20                  ms
                                     tPSON_L H min                   PSON_L minimum High time                    10                                 ms

                                                                                  Table 3. AC Turn-on / Dip Timing


  8.8 PWOK_H SIGNAL
     The PWOK_H is an open drain output with an internal pull-up to 3.3 V indicating whether both VSB and V1 outputs are within
     regulation. This pin is active-low. The timing diagram is shown in Figure 26 / Figure 29 and referenced in the Table 6.

